{"duration_api_ms":36800,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"a8e2f2ae-df9e-4627-b5da-8c69bab1dc16","total_cost_usd":2.7142314,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":323500,"cache_read_input_tokens":197277,"output_tokens":4338,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1427},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":323500,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":554,"cache_read_input_tokens":197277,"cache_creation_input_tokens":85295,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":85295},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":4338,"cacheReadInputTokens":197277,"cacheCreationInputTokens":323500,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.7142314,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1427,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":2,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I've written the labels to `labels/coder-1.json`. Robin Vos codes to **rung 5, \"Require parental permission before staff use a different name or pronouns.\"** That chair rests on a single source, AB 103 (2025).\n\n- **AB 103 (2025), the basis for the chair.** He voted Y as Speaker on passage, which carried 50–43. This is a single-subject bill. Its operative section says staff may not use a name or pronouns that do not match a minor's biological sex \"without written authorization from the pupil’s parent or legal guardian\". That matches every clause of rung 5, so I coded both passages (vote page and bill text) `chair-shaped`.\n- **AB 510 (2024) and AB 963 (2022), supporting only.** He voted Y on both. Each contains a \"right to determine the names and pronouns used for the child while at school\", but alongside many unrelated parental rights. I coded them `multi-subject`: they point the same way but can't carry a chair, and they are not in `rests_on`.\n\nThere are no quotes, because no source contains Vos's own words.\n\nThree things a reviewer should check:\n- **Actor quote.** Each vote page records the vote as `Y SPEAKER R`. The only link to Vos by name is the page header \"Speaker Vos\", so the actor quote relies on the Speaker being him.\n- **Bill version.** The AB 103 text in the sources is the introduced version. I listed the engrossed, as-passed text in `needs_source` to confirm the provision didn't change before the vote.\n- **Term dates.** His current term dates are unknown in the person record. I coded all the votes `in-term` without being able to check that against dates.","ttft_ms":14564,"type":"result","duration_ms":38952,"uuid":"01c64141-6d79-4ad0-9b07-233a6036f408","ttft_stream_ms":1859,"time_to_request_ms":236,"first_content_frame_ms":1859,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
